Topic: Installation of Packet Tracer and Basic Connections

Today was my second day of learning computer networking. I learned how to install Cisco Packet Tracer and how to create basic network connections using PCs and a router.

First, I installed Cisco Packet Tracer on my system. The installation process was simple, and after completing it, I opened the application and explored the interface. I understood where the devices are located, such as routers, switches, PCs, and cables. This helped me feel more comfortable using the tool.

Next, I practiced creating a simple network. I added PCs and a router from the device panel into the workspace. After that, I connected the PCs to the router using the correct cables. I learned the importance of choosing the right cable type while making connections.

Then, I configured basic settings like assigning IP addresses to the PCs and checking the connections. I also tested the network to see whether the PCs could communicate through the router. This practical activity helped me understand how devices connect and communicate in a real network.

Overall, today’s session was very useful. Packet Tracer helped me understand networking concepts visually and practically. I feel more confident now and excited to learn more advanced networking topics in the next sessions.
